#: ../../../debug.rst:5
msgid "Debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:7
msgid "Xonsh supports two complementary ways to debug xonsh code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:9
msgid ""
"**Debug in IDE** — attach a full graphical debugger from an editor like VS "
"Code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:11
msgid ""
"**Instant debugging** — drop into a debugger at the exact call site with ``@."
"debug``, with automatic engine selection and a xonsh-syntax REPL when no "
"external debugger is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:16
msgid "Debug in IDE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:18
msgid ""
"Xonsh extension for VS Code provides syntax highlighting and basic language "
"support for ``.xsh`` files. Install via the extensions menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:22
msgid "Instant debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:24
msgid ""
"When you need to stop execution at a specific call site without wiring up an "
"IDE, xonsh ships a debugging helper attached to every session as ``@."
"debug``. It works like Python's builtin ``breakpoint()``, but with automatic "
"engine selection, session-aware fallbacks, and a xonsh-syntax REPL when no "
"external debugger is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:31
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:33
msgid "Drop into a debugger at any point in your xonsh code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:35
msgid "@.debug.breakpoint()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:39
msgid ""
"The engine is chosen automatically in priority order: ``pdbp`` → ``ipdb`` → "
"``pdb`` → ``execer`` → ``eval``. The first one that is importable (or, for "
"``execer``, available on the session) wins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:44
msgid "To force a specific engine for a single call:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:46
msgid ""
"@.debug.breakpoint(engine='pdbp')\n"
"@.debug.breakpoint(engine='ipdb')\n"
"@.debug.breakpoint(engine='pdb')\n"
"@.debug.breakpoint(engine='execer')   # xonsh REPL at the call site\n"
"@.debug.breakpoint(engine='eval')     # plain-Python REPL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:55
msgid "Setting the Default Engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:57
msgid ""
"Set ``$XONSH_DEBUG_BREAKPOINT_ENGINE`` in your :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` to "
"change the default used when ``engine`` is not passed (or is ``'auto'``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:60
msgid "$XONSH_DEBUG_BREAKPOINT_ENGINE = 'pdbp'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:64
msgid ""
"Allowed values: ``'auto'`` (default), ``'pdbp'``, ``'ipdb'``, ``'pdb'``, "
"``'execer'``, ``'eval'``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:67
msgid "An explicit argument to ``breakpoint()`` always beats the env var."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:70
msgid "Wrapping breakpoint() in a helper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:72
msgid ""
"If you build your own dev-helper that calls ``@.debug.breakpoint()`` for "
"you, the debugger would normally stop *inside* the helper, which is rarely "
"what you want. Pass an explicit ``frame=`` to relocate the stop site to any "
"frame on the stack — typically the helper's caller. This mirrors ``pdbp."
"set_trace(frame=...)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:78
msgid ""
"@ def my_dev_helper():\n"
"     print(\"dropping in…\")\n"
"     @.debug.breakpoint(frame=@.imp.sys._getframe().f_back)\n"
"@ my_dev_helper()\n"
"dropping in…\n"
"BREAKPOINT WITH 'pdbp'\n"
"# …debugger now sits at my_dev_helper's caller, not inside the helper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:88
msgid ""
"When ``frame=`` is omitted (the default), the debugger uses the immediate "
"caller's frame, exactly as before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:92
msgid "Engines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:98
msgid "Engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:99
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:100
msgid "``pdbp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:101
msgid ""
"`pdbp <https://github.com/mdmintz/pdbp>`_ — enhanced pdb (sticky mode, "
"syntax highlighting, ``where``/``u``/``d`` frame hiding). Install with "
"``xpip install pdbp``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:104
msgid "``ipdb``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:105
msgid ""
"`ipdb <https://github.com/gotcha/ipdb>`_ - IPython-flavored pdb. Install "
"with ``xpip install ipdb``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:106
msgid "``pdb``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:107
msgid "Stdlib ``pdb``. Always available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:108
msgid "``execer``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:109
msgid ""
"A REPL at the caller's frame backed by the session's :class:`~xonsh.execer."
"Execer`. Full xonsh syntax is available — subprocesses (``ls``, ``$(ls)``), "
"env lookups (``@.env['HOME']``), aliases, and ``@.`` attribute access. "
"Raises ``RuntimeError`` if no execer is attached to the session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:114
msgid "``eval``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:115
msgid ""
"A minimal REPL using plain Python ``eval``/``exec``. Has no dependency on a "
"xonsh session — works in detached contexts (scripts, tests) the same as "
"inside an interactive shell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:119
msgid ""
"When ``engine='auto'`` resolves to an engine, ``@.debug`` prints a short "
"banner identifying the choice and a one-line hint about how to continue or "
"abort, then drops into that engine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:124
msgid "Tab completion in callable aliases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:126
msgid ""
"xonsh runs callable aliases (registered via ``@aliases.register``) in worker "
"threads. CPython only wires ``readline`` into the main thread, so the "
"``pdbp``, ``ipdb``, and ``pdb`` engines lose tab completion when invoked "
"from inside an alias — the ``TAB`` key inserts a literal tab into the "
"underlying ``input()`` call instead of triggering completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:132
msgid ""
"When ``engine='auto'`` is resolved from a non-main thread, ``@.debug`` auto-"
"walks past the readline-based engines and selects ``execer`` (or ``eval`` if "
"no session is attached). Both REPLs use ``input()`` directly with no "
"completion, so the missing ``TAB`` matches the prompt and there is no false "
"expectation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:138
msgid ""
"If you set ``$XONSH_DEBUG_BREAKPOINT_ENGINE`` or pass ``engine=`` to one of "
"the readline-based engines, ``@.debug`` still honours your choice from a "
"worker thread but prints a :class:`UserWarning` so the broken ``TAB`` is not "
"surprising. The warning is informational — pdbp/ipdb/pdb still work, just "
"without tab completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:144
msgid "This is a CPython limitation, not a xonsh bug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:147
msgid "REPL Commands (execer and eval engines)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:149
msgid ""
"Both ``execer`` and ``eval`` engines start a small REPL at the caller's "
"frame. The REPL accepts any Python/xonsh expression or statement, and "
"recognizes the following control commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:157
msgid "Command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:158
msgid "Effect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:159
msgid "``c`` / ``cont`` / ``continue``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:160
msgid "Resume execution after the breakpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:161
msgid "``exit`` / ``quit`` / ``q``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:162
msgid ""
"Abort execution — raises :class:`xonsh.debug.XonshDebugQuit`, which "
"propagates out of the ``breakpoint()`` call and unwinds the stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:164
msgid "``EOF`` / ``Ctrl-C``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:165
msgid "Same as ``continue`` (least destructive default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:167
msgid ""
"Expression results are printed automatically. Statements (assignments, "
"loops, etc.) run in the caller's frame, so local variables are visible and "
"modifiable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:171
msgid ""
"execer> @.env['HOME']\n"
"'/Users/you'\n"
"execer> ls *.py | head -3\n"
"debug.py\n"
"environ.py\n"
"tools.py\n"
"execer> my_local_var = 42\n"
"execer> c"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:183
msgid "Routing Python's builtin ``breakpoint()`` Through ``@.debug``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:185
msgid ""
"PEP 553 makes Python's builtin ``breakpoint()`` go through ``sys."
"breakpointhook``. ``@.debug`` can install a hook that routes every builtin "
"``breakpoint()`` call through the same engine as ``@.debug.breakpoint()``. "
"Add the following to your :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:191
msgid ""
"$XONSH_DEBUG_BREAKPOINT_ENGINE = 'pdbp'\n"
"@.debug.replace_builtin_breakpoint()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:196
msgid ""
"After this, ``breakpoint()`` anywhere in xonsh code — or in any plain Python "
"module loaded inside the session — drops into the configured engine at the "
"call site. To restore Python's default behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../debug.rst:200
msgid ""
"import sys\n"
"sys.breakpointhook = sys.__breakpointhook__"
msgstr ""
